kardinal promotes versions of your application through environments, with
gates, pull requests and health checks, on Kubernetes.

Getting started:
  kardinal quickstart --repo <your fork>                 try it on a local cluster
  kardinal init --name my-app --repo <gitops repo>       write a Pipeline for your repository
  kardinal ship my-app --image app:1.4 --wait            ship a version and follow it
  kardinal why my-app prod                               why it waits, and what moves it on

Usage:
  kardinal [command]

Get started:
  dashboard      Open the kardinal UI dashboard in a browser
  doctor         Run pre-flight checks to verify the cluster is correctly configured
  init           Write a Pipeline for your GitOps repository, from flags or a few questions
  quickstart     Install kardinal on a local cluster and promote a first version
  version        Print the CLI, controller, and kro (Graph) versions

Ship and observe:
  create         Create kardinal resources
  diff           Show what changes between two versions (Bundles)
  get            Display one or more kardinal resources
  history        Show a pipeline's promotion history, newest first
  logs           Show promotion step execution logs for a pipeline
  ship           Ship a version: create a Bundle, and with --wait follow it
  status         Show controller health or per-pipeline in-flight promotion details
  why            Say why an environment waits, and what moves it on

Approve and gate:
  approve        Approve (or reject) the version waiting for an environment's approval gates
  inbox          List what waits for a person: on you first, then on others
  override       Force-pass a PolicyGate with a mandatory audit record
  policy         Manage and evaluate promotion policy gates
  promote        Promote the version verified upstream into an environment
  verify         Record a verdict on the version running in an environment (verify gates)

Incident:
  freeze         Freeze agents, or stop the line for everyone; with no flags, list the freezes
  hold           Keep an environment on what runs there now
  pause          Pause a pipeline, or one fleet: no new promotion steps start
  reject         Reject a version: it is never promoted again, and rollback never picks it
  resume         Resume a paused pipeline, or a paused fleet
  rollback       Roll back an environment to the version before
  unfreeze       Lift a freeze
  unhold         Release an environment's hold (kardinal hold, or rollback --hold)

Admin and debug:
  audit          Audit log commands: view and summarize promotion events
  completion     Generate shell completion scripts
  delete         Delete kardinal resources
  help           Help about any command
  mcp            Serve kardinal to an AI agent over MCP (stdio)
  metrics        Show promotion metrics (DORA-style) for a pipeline
  refresh        Force re-reconciliation of a Pipeline
  validate       Validate Pipeline and PolicyGate YAML before applying to the cluster
  verify-receipt Verify a signed promotion receipt: its signature, subject, environment and levels

Flags:
      --context string      Kubeconfig context override
  -h, --help                help for kardinal
      --kubeconfig string   Path to kubeconfig file (default: $KUBECONFIG, else ~/.kube/config)
  -n, --namespace string    Kubernetes namespace (default: current context namespace)
  -o, --output string       Output format: table (default), json, yaml, wide (json and yaml: create bundle, get auditevents, get bundles, get pipelines, get steps, get subscriptions, history, hold, inbox, promote, rollback, ship, status, unhold, verify-receipt, why; wide: get subscriptions, status, why)

Use "kardinal [command] --help" for more information about a command.
